[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Authored full unit-test module for semver_solver_impl: VersionEngine parse_version/compare_precedence/parse_range/satisfies happy paths plus contracted InvalidVersionError/InvalidRangeError preconditions, wildcard/caret/tilde/hyphen/union and prerelease filter/inequality branches; PackageRepository register/get/has/all with descending ordering, copy isolation and PackageNotFoundError; DependencySolver highest-precedence transitive resolution, backtracking, missing-package and unsatisfiable ResolutionConflictError via protocol-conforming mocked collaborators within active lifecycle phase scopes.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implemented the SemVer interface module: non-frozen dataclass error hierarchy (SemVerError and subclasses with __str__ delegating to message), immutable @data_type records Version/VersionRange/PackageDependency/PackageRelease/ResolutionOutcome, concrete Version methods (is_prerelease, canonical format, __str__), ComparatorOp enum, and @poly_type protocol stubs for VersionEngine, PackageRepository, and DependencySolver matching the low-level specification.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implemented the SemVer engine, repository, and dependency solver: regex-based SemVer 2.0.0 parsing with leading-zero rejection, full precedence comparison (numeric/prerelease/build-ignoring), range compilation to DNF covering comparators, wildcards, caret/tilde expansion, hyphen ranges, unions, operator whitespace tolerance, comma/empty/bare-partial rejection, and prerelease filtering semantics; repository with descending precedence sorted release storage, PackageNotFoundError, membership queries; MRV-ordered backtracking resolver using get_singleton collaborators that backtracks on conflicts, records derivation steps/conflict trails, and raises ResolutionConflictError without leaking PackageNotFoundError.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax] [viol:post.wrong_return] Facet: original malformed range text in diagnostic. Witness: input='   ', exp='   ', obs=''. In VersionEngine.parse_range the caller-supplied range text is stripped before compilation, and the error helper receives only that stripped text, so InvalidRangeError.raw_range is populated with the trimmed expression instead of the original malformed range expression named by the contract; for whitespace-only input the original expression is replaced by the empty string. The rejection itself occurs, but the contracted structured payload must retain the exact original malformed expression text supplied by the caller.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Fixed parse_range diagnostic payload: VersionEngine.parse_range now passes the exact caller-supplied range text to range compilation (which trims internally only for parsing) so InvalidRangeError.raw_range preserves the original malformed expression, including whitespace-only input, rather than the trimmed value; VersionRange.raw_text still stores the trimmed canonical expression. Audited sibling error sites (parse_version, get_releases, resolve) for the same original-text-payload pattern.
